    "recommendations": "Providing the property with a clearly marked, well-identified address visible from the access road could improve responder navigation, particularly given the single entry point and extended driveway approach. Ensuring the driveway width and overhead clearance along its full length would support apparatus movement and reduce delays during emergency operations. Where dense vegetation borders the driveway or walkways, maintaining adequate clearance along travel corridors may enhance responder movement toward both the main building and the detached structure. Given limited rear access, identifying and communicating any secondary pedestrian pathways to the rear of the property in advance could assist responders in establishing tactical positioning during an incident."
